## Raise dependency floors for Pillow and certifi advisories
================================================================================

Context: Dependabot reported 28 Pillow advisories, including three critical
image-decoder issues, plus a critical certifi compromised-root advisory in
both application lockfiles. Pillow 13 is the first patched release and drops
end-of-life Python 3.10, so the supported runtime floor moves to Python 3.11.

Changes:

1. pyproject.toml and uv.lock
   Require Python 3.11, Pillow 13.0.0, and certifi 2026.10.19; refresh the
   frozen security entries without downgrading matplotlib.
2. src/mcp-server/pyproject.toml and src/mcp-server/uv.lock
   Apply the certifi 2026.10.19 security floor to the standalone MCP graph.
3. README.md and docs/
   Align installation, deployment, development, architecture, product, and
   contribution guidance with the Python 3.11 runtime floor.

